Chapter 18
When a ratio lies: currency, inflation, a change of method — and the verdict
حين يكذب المؤشر: العملة والتضخم وتغير السياسة — ثم الحكم النهائي
Seventeen chapters have built ratios and believed them. This one asks when they cannot be believed, and then does the thing the whole of Book 1 has been preparing for: it reaches a verdict on a company using all of them at once.
Three forces can move a ratio with nothing happening in the business. An exchange rate can change, and a company with foreign operations will report different numbers for an unchanged subsidiary. Inflation can erode the comparability of a balance sheet carried at historical cost. And the company can change an accounting treatment, which moves the figures and must be adjusted for before any comparison. All three are examinable in their own right, and all three are reasons the last section of this chapter is written with care rather than confidence.
Figure F518-01 is your map.
Figure F518-01. Chapter 18 roadmap: three ways a ratio misleads, the general limitations, and the verdict.
