LANGUAGE FOCUS   "Material"
English material in accounting does not mean physical or important in a general sense: it means large enough that its omission or misstatement could change a user's decision. It is a threshold, and it is deliberately relative to the entity. Arabic uses جوهري, which carries the same sense of going to the essence rather than to the size. French uses significatif — note that it does not mean significant in the statistical sense, and that matériel in French means equipment, so a literal translation of material misstatement is a sentence about machinery. The exam uses the word in its accounting sense every time, and a candidate who reads it as important loses the threshold idea that makes it useful.
